(Start|Action|Review|Closeout)|IndexGeneration|IndexFederatedMaterial|IndexInput|ReviewExecutable|GovernanceReadViewExternalABA' -count=1 2>&1 | tail -15","timeout":600000,"description":"Build, vet, run focused domain tests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MTsHLDnEcFhSaenEcsk92L","tool_input":{"command":"go -C /tmp/pose-review-run-3263644701/worktree/pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'GovernanceReadViewProbe|GovernanceReadViewDirtyToDirtySnapshot|GovernanceReadViewGit|GovernanceReadViewProjection|GovernanceReadViewLocalProjection|ObligationProjection|GovernanceWriteGuard|IndexFederatedMaterial|IndexInput|ReviewExecutable|GovernanceReadViewExternalABA' -count=1","timeout":600000,"description":"Run focused B34 domain tests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01W5bLV4nXpqzTPycGQj6Lbk","tool_input":{"command":"git -C /tmp/pose-review-run-3263644701/worktree diff 42c8891f..448a7504 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go","description":"Show D9 executable hash diff"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WteW7QznaWf7oUjX4KKw8K","tool_input":{"command":"pose review-check spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation","timeout":300000,"description":"Run read-only POSE review check"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":44,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Decision: changes-requested.** I found one blocking defect and two low-severity follow-ups.\n\nI couldn't execute anything except a few early read-only git commands; the session denied every `go test` and `pose` command. So the mechanical criteria below rest on the sealed evidence plus my own reading of the code. I did not re-run any of it. Any tool with no sealed evidence is marked `not-used`, not passed.\n\n## Blocking defect\n\n**F1 (medium, blocker): a change to the authorized-root registry during the final audit never reaches `read_view.freshness`.**\n- **Where it's detected:** the final audit in `pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:388-398` finds the change (or a final-audit budget overrun). It records it only in the returned audit (`ChangedPaths: \"authorized-roots\"`, `ChangedProducers[\"projection\"]`).\n- **Where it's lost:** the operation's `metadata()` at `governance_read_view.go:428-529` builds freshness, limitations and the ID only from the per-root audits, `rootOverflow` and the registry overflow seen at the start (`registryOverflow`). It ignores this result.\n- **Effect on review/closeout:** after the single retry, `withGovernanceReviewReadViewAttempt` (`review_closeout.go:464-471`) attaches metadata that still says `current`. `applyReviewReadView` (`:549`) and `applyCloseoutReadView` (`:595`) then return early, so approval and terminal status stand even though the audit saw a change. That breaks R3 (\"interleaving → incoherent/unknown, never relabel\") and the milestone exit gate.\n- **Effect on the projection:** `projectObligations` reports `snapshot.coherent=false` alongside `read_view.freshness: \"current\"`, which is inconsistent.\n- **Not affected:** `ObligationSnapshotChanges` (it checks `Coherent`) and the index capture path (it reads the audit directly).\n- **No test covers it:** \"authorized root registry changed\" and \"authorized-roots\" appear nowhere in any test.\n\n## Follow-ups (low)\n- **F2:** `governance_read_view.go:2065`. The final audit deep-copies every captured byte, so peak memory is roughly twice the 512 MiB input budget plus the file being re-read. The calibrated corpus of ~370 MB would hold about 740 MB+ at peak.\n- **F3:** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go:205`. The `federated-roadmap` error code is picked by matching a substring of the error text instead of a typed error.\n\n## Criteria\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | The spec (§3, the A→B→A paragraph) and the ADR separate verified facts from the external-writer/ABA limit; tech-debt INCOMPLETE is kept |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration (run with `-race`); lease and lock order in `governance_write_guard.go:132-187,472-528` |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration; report stays at schema v1, `read_view` is additive |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration; typed guard errors at `governance_write_guard.go:23-65` |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test; bounded summaries without paths at `governance_read_view_capture.go:88-137` |\n| compatibility | passed | `POSE.md:372`; golden tool catalog; v1 schemas kept |\n| correctness | **finding (F1)** | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration (doesn't cover the registry path) |\n| cross-component-integration | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration |\n| design-causality | passed | D2/D4/D7 extend `Files` with per-operation capture, final audit and a guarded write; the digest now binds observed bytes |\n| documentation | passed | `POSE.md:372-373`, the ADR, the MCP catalog |\n| milestone exit gate | **finding (F1)** | an interleaving can be labelled `current` at the review/closeout gate |\n| operability | passed | `index_generation_build.go:39-51`; guard errors are actionable |\n| requirements | **finding (F1)** | R3/R5 lack evidence for the root-registry interleaving |\n| scope | passed | changed files match the spec's artifact list |\n| security | passed | lock-path symlink checks at `governance_write_guard.go:437-548`; root digests instead of paths; D8 excludes the live policy |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | extends `Files` rather than adding a daemon, cache or snapshot; F2 is the noted cost |\n\n## Structural facts\n- **SD-0cf58a00** (`validation-matrix.json`): caused by R10 and Validation V7 / the deterministic checks. It adds the required race check `governance-read-view-integration` and the explicit `-count=1` build/test/vet (`replaceDefaultChecks`), as recorded in the execution log for ba458666.\n- **SD-5e72492d** (the ADR): caused by the spec constraint \"O ADR B34 deve ser aceito antes de alterar o contrato\" (\"the B34 ADR must be accepted before the contract changes\"). It is the basis for decisions D2–D9.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\", \"line\": 388, \"summary\": \"Operation final audit records an authorized-root registry change/overflow only in the returned audit; governanceReadViewOperation.metadata (lines 428-529) derives freshness/limitations/ID from per-root audits and initial overflow flags only, so after the single retry review/closeout (review_closeout.go:464-471, 549, 595) keep approval/terminal with read_view.freshness=current and projection reports coherent=false with freshness current. No test covers this path.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\", \"line\": 2065, \"summary\": \"Final audit deep-copies all retained captured bytes, doubling resident memory (up to ~2x the 512 MiB input budget) during audit.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go\", \"line\": 205, \"summary\": \"Index build failure code 'federated-roadmap' is selected by substring match on error text instead of a typed/sentinel error.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:34\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:POSE.md:372\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md:97\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:POSE.md:372\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-state-consistency-and-recovery-governance-read-view\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:549\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go:39\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_write_guard.go:437\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:36\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution was denied in this review session and no sealed evidence ID covers this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-32b95cbf2ff92ef6\", \"rationale\": \"\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; command execution denied; no sealed evidence for it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; command execution denied; no sealed evidence for it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied; integration inventory is static and has no sealed evidence ID.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; command execution denied; implementer reports INCOMPLETE (two unreadable historical specs).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied; no sealed evidence for this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"knowledge-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied; no sealed evidence for this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied (attempted); no sealed evidence for this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; command execution denied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; command execution denied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied; no sealed evidence for this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed evidence covers only the pose-mcp module checks; no sealed global validation result for this checkpoint.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The tests module declares replaceDefaultChecks with an empty check list (producer coverage none); no sealed evidence exists for it.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1603,"type":"result","duration_ms":195512,"uuid":"8a8922c6-7521-48b3-b519-b1288172f96c","ttft_stream_ms":888,"time_to_request_ms":150,"first_content_frame_ms":888,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":80,"outputTokens":19811,"cacheReadInputTokens":2965502,"cacheCreationInputTokens":111421,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.8810083999999991,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8352,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hIn